Ok, I'm ready to do battle; teleport down to level 50, 
check my mirror, 'You sense a powerful wizard above you', and start up.
I hit level 49, and there aren't any stairs at all - up or down!
I traverse the maze twice, stepping on every square, pulverizing boulders
just in case one is obscuring the stairwell, but nope.  Luckily, I
have a blank scroll.  Unluckily, I don't have a magic marker.  So, to
kill time, I start destroying the walls in the maze.  About half way
through,  a vampire lord drops a magic marker.  Scroll of teleportation
now on hand, but no way to confuse myself, so I keep hacking at the 
walls until I have turned the entire maze into a Big Room.  I check the
level again -- still no stairs.  Finally, an Umber Hulk shows up, 
confusion ensues, and I teleport up.

Anyone else ever been on a level with _no_ stairs?


